From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 11:05:27 -0647
Subject: [PATCH] scsi: ufs: exynos: zumapro: Hold the device in reset across
 suspend

gs101 and gs201 drive the UFS device's reset low in their suspend hook
(gs101_ufs_suspend()), as Google's driver does on zuma, and the host
enable on resume pulses it high again. zumapro had no suspend hook, so
the device went into system suspend with its reset released.

On the Pixel 9a one resume in a run of four lost the link: "link
startup failed 1" through every retry, then
"ufshcd_host_reset_and_restore: Host init failed", every later read
failing with DID_ERROR, and the root file system read-only. With the
reset held low through suspend, as on gs101, 32 s2idle cycles with RTC
wakes in a row resumed clean.

Signed-off-by: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/ufs/host/ufs-exynos.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-exynos.c b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-exynos.c
index 2860b1b01..61078ad79 100644
--- a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-exynos.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-exynos.c
@@ -2558,6 +2558,7 @@ static const struct exynos_ufs_drv_data zumapro_ufs_drvs = {
 				  EXYNOS_UFS_OPT_UNGATE_POST_CHANGE,
 	.iocc_mask		= UFS_GS101_SHARABLE,
 	.drv_init		= zumapro_ufs_drv_init,
+	.suspend		= gs101_ufs_suspend,
 	.pre_link		= zumapro_ufs_pre_link,
 	.post_link		= zumapro_ufs_post_link,
 	.pre_pwr_change		= zumapro_ufs_pre_pwr_change,
